# TRACE-ONLY OVERLAY: lane crossings do not end an exploration-trace segment
# (user 2026-11-01, "can we fix crossings in" -> "yes").
#
# WHY. Crossings ended 102 of the deterministic Town02 trace's 134 segments
# (median segment 11 m), only because the trace inherited the eval's fault
# rule. Nothing is scored in a trace -- it exists to build a map -- so the car
# may cross a line and drive on; going OFF THE ROAD or a COLLISION still ends
# the segment exactly as before.
#
# WHAT CHANGES. Only termination. The base is the checkpoint's own training
# overlay, sourced first, and nothing here touches what reaches the policy: its
# observations are camera images and the reward never does, so its behaviour
# is identical -- only when an episode stops differs. run_trace's own fault
# check skips crossings via TRACE_END_ON_CROSSING=0 (set by the launcher).
#
# THE COST, stated rather than hidden: the policy never learned what to do
# after a crossing (in training one always ended the episode), so afterwards it
# may drive on in the wrong lane. Those frames are still on the road, so their
# positions are valid map locations; each segment records its crossing count.
#
# NOT FOR TRAINING. ROUTE_RETREAT_SCALE goes back to 1 because gated_reward
# refuses a discounted retreat when crossings are not terminal (approach-
# retreat becomes farmable). That guard protects LEARNING; a trace learns
# nothing, and the retreat scale only changes the recorded reward.
. "$REPO/${TRACE_BASE_OVERLAY:-slurm/v30_overlay.env}"
export EXPLORE_LANE_MODE=penalise
unset ROUTE_PROGRESS_POSITIVE
export ROUTE_RETREAT_SCALE=1
